there are a lot of clever moments and  uncomfortable subtext than the original  Back to the Future that flew right over  your head if you watched it when you  were a kid from rock-and-roll nods the  Freudian subplots here are things that  only adults notice and back to the  future as strange as it might be for a  cool rock and roll skateboard team to  form a lasting friendship with a  middle-aged science weirdo the emotional  core back to the future is definitely  Marty McFly's relationship with Doc  Brown but believe it or not the  relationship that likely inspired Marty  and Doc's friendship is even weirder  Marty's out of his depth impulsiveness  and Doc's blunt knowledge bear a  striking resemblance to mr. Peabody and  Sherman the stars of a segment from the  Rocky and Bullwinkle show about a genius  talking dog and his young friend  traveling through time well actually  it's a time machine if that connection  seems like a stretch consider that when  Marty travels back to 1955 the first  thing he does is crash into a farm house  owned by the Peabody family and while  he's not named in the film the credits  identified the boy who assumes he's an  alien as Sherman it's a fun reference  but maybe it's also the reason why the  actual first time traveler in the film  is Einstein Doc Brown's faithful dog one  of the most appealing parts of the movie  especially for children is Marty getting  to meet his parents when they were his  age instead of inscrutable authority  figures Marty's parents in 1955 are is  awkward goofy peers seeing them at that  age isn't just weird for Marty it  reminds the younger audience that their  parents were young once two less  wholesome especially two adults are the  extremely uncomfortable scenes in which  Marty's mother tries to seduce him the  incestuous subtext that Marty having to  fend off his mother's advances and the  fact that her crush on him is enough to  threaten the entire timeline could keep  Sigmund Freud busy for years like in  kissing back to future is great for a  lot of reasons but the climactic musical  performance that Marty puts on at the  prom is a highlight and a movie full of  them it brings character beats and  offhand lines full circle as Marty  finally gets to play on stage in front  of his whole high school although about  30 years earlier than he hoped while  assuring that his parents get together  and that he gets to keep existing it's a  great scene pack  full of great references most fans got  the joke that Chuck Berry's cousin calls  him to let him know about Johnny be good  but Marty also emulates Eddie Van Halen  Jimi Hendrix and Angus Young from ac/dc  touch is added by Michael J Fox that  said as a grown-up you might think it's  a little weird for this movie to suggest  that rock-and-roll was actually invented  by a white suburban teen and then copied  by black artists in the 50s that's  pretty weird right Marty really gets put  through the wringer trying to get his  parents to hook up after he accidentally  interrupts their meet-cute in 1955 one  of the most inventive trixie polls is to  pretend to be an alien and threaten  George with death if he doesn't ask  Laraine out since Marty knows that  George is a bit of a science fiction  geek he announces his fake alien persona  was some pretty familiar names an  extraterrestrial from the planet bumpkin  by the end of the movie George has even  written a novel that based on the cover  design is at least partly inspired by  the meeting it's a cute gang but in the  world of Back to the Future  did George start writing about Darth  Vader and Vulcan in the 50s years before  Star Wars and Star Trek were released  does the McFly family's new prosperity  come from a lawsuit against George Lucas  claiming copyright infringement from  George's work and if not what did he  think when two of the most popular  sci-fi stories started referencing his  own alien encounter it's pretty easy to  imagine adult George McFly attending  sci-fi conventions trying to snag a few  precious seconds with Lucas and Gene  Roddenberry to confirm they were visited  by the strange alien 2 while it seems  like a happy ending the final moments a  back to the future are much darker than  his apparent at first glance Marty's got  in the truck of his dreams his brother  is wearing a suit to work instead of  slacking off at home and his mom and dad  seem a whole lot happier and much more  well off the thing is Marty comes from  the timeline that we see back at the  beginning of the film and he has strong  memories of what his family used to be  like before he started messing around  with the space-time continuum if you  think about it for a moment it becomes  existentially horrifying when you  remember that Marty doesn't really know  these people they look like his family  and act like an improved version of his  family but they reference moments that  never had  into this Marty leaving him confused  when he compares them to the people he  left just yesterday in 1985 imagine  having an entire life that's similar but  decidedly different from the one you  remember imagine sitting down with your  family as they make references to events  from your childhood that are just close  enough to leave you with deja vu but not  enough to spur any actual memories of  the event in question  Marty's old family with all their  problems and personality flaws are  pretty much dead replaced by strangers  who have had entire lives that he can't  remember  it's amazing that Back to the Future 2  didn't take place entirely in a  therapist office  [Music]
 

